; generated-format instantiation 2026-08-08
|term[value-object]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A thing that IS its description; cannot dangle, rename, or change.
  :dual-of @entity
  :source-type external
  :external-equivalent close:ddd-value-object
  |designation value-object
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-entities-values-promises
    :anchor entity-value-object
    :projection paraphrase
    A thing that is its description. Two value objects with the same content are not similar — they are the same, and "which one" is a meaningless question. A "changed" value object is a different value object.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:v_1 = v_2 \iff desc(v_1) = desc(v_2)>
    :reading Identity IS extensional equality of description; a hash is a complete description compressed into designator shape.
  |set-rel :kind disjoint-from :to @entity
  |example
    The number 47; the exact bytes of a file at a commit; a git blob.
